  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rSTAV-PL01, STAV-PL02 existing site plan, STAV-PL02 existing and proposed block plan, Location Plan 1:1250 PP14251352v1, Design & Access Statement, Energy Statement, CIL form, Short stay cycle stand, Velo store, Highway Safety Impact Form, Flood Risk Assessment.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Within three months of the date of this decision, bicycle parking facilities should be provided in accordance with drawing STAV-PL02 dated 06.06.2025 and as a minimum as follows:\r\ro Provision of FOUR long stay cycle parking spaces\ro in an accessible location: the access route to the store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gate (excluding the store door).\ro secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob\ro fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof\r\rIf provision is not made, the occupation of the development shall cease.  Upon implementation, the approved bicycle parking facilities specified in this condition shall be permanently retained. In the event of a legal challenge to this decision, or to a decision made pursuant to the procedure set out in this condition, the operation of the time limits specified in this condition shall be suspended until that legal challenge has been finally determined. \r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.\r",
    "Within three months of the date of this permission, refuse and waste storage and recycling facilities shall be provided within the curtilage of the application site as required by the standards of the Council. Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and to ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.\r",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition. \r \rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area. \r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than five residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate \r"
  ],
